# Mtengatenga AR Museum App - Development Rules

## Project Context
This is a Flutter mobile app for Mtengatenga Cultural Museum in Malawi.
Core features: AR artifact scanning, AI guide, indoor navigation, digital ticketing.

## Architecture
- **OOP/Clean Architecture**: Domain entities, repositories, services
- **Offline-first**: Supabase + local SQLite caching
- **State Management**: (add Riverpod/Bloc when we introduce it)

## Coding Standards
- Use Dart 3.0+ features
- All classes must have clear single responsibilities
- Repository pattern for all data access
- Domain entities are immutable and isolated from UI
- UI models are separate from domain entities (use mappers)

## File Structure
lib/
  core/
    domain/entities/     - Pure business objects
    data/repositories/   - Data access interfaces + implementations
    data/mappers/        - Domain ↔ UI model converters
    services/            - Infrastructure (Supabase, locators)
    models/              - UI presentation models
  features/              - Feature modules (home, scan, artifact, etc.)
  theme/                 - Design tokens

## Current Phase
Building core data layer with Supabase backend.
Next: populate real artifact content and add offline caching.

## Key Dependencies
- supabase_flutter: Backend + auth
- flutter_dotenv: Environment config
- (future) brick_offline_first_with_supabase: Offline caching
- (future) ar_flutter_plugin: AR scanning

## Don't
- Never hardcode Supabase credentials (use .env)
- Don't mix UI and domain logic
- Don't access Supabase directly from widgets (use repositories)
- Don't commit .env files to git
